<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stamp Act Congress</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1765">1765</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Stamp Act Congress met in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> City in October 1765, with delegates from nine British American colonies, to oppose the Stamp Act. It adopted a Declaration of Rights and Grievances asserting that only the colonists' own assemblies could tax them, and sent petitions to the king and Parliament. It was the first joint colonial action against British policy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stamp-act-congress.jpg" alt="Stamp Act Congress" width="265" height="362" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: not listed · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1765_one_penny_stamp.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
